(FLW-39: "All resources are automatically cleaned up before exit"
 (LANGUAGE.md:2350). Not assertable from inside the exiting program -
 there is no observation point after Exit - so this probe records the
 half that IS observable, out of band: it writes to a file handle it
 never closes, then exits 3, and the bytes are on disk afterwards.
 Hand-checked when the probe was written:
   $ rm -f /tmp/vox-flw-cleanup.txt; ./p; echo $?
   3
   $ cat /tmp/vox-flw-cleanup.txt
   flushed on exit
 check-probes.sh can only verify the exit status here; the file half has
 to be looked at by hand.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox FLW-39.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   exit 3
)
open a file for writing called sink at "/tmp/vox-flw-cleanup.txt".
Write "flushed on exit" to sink.
Exit 3.
